From: qlattice hardening audit (task-42)
Subject: [PATCH] CartesianStencil: do not take &v[0] of an empty surface list

BuildSurfaceList() computes surface_list_size = 0 on a single-rank grid
(all stencil points are node-local), then unconditionally passes
&surface_list_host[0] and &surface_list[0] to acceleratorCopyToDevice().
Taking operator[](0) on an empty std::vector is UB; libc++ hardening
(nixpkgs default -D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_FAST)
turns it into __builtin_verbose_trap (SIGTRAP on aarch64-darwin,
SIGILL on x86) while constructing a Wilson/Mobius fermion operator on a
single-rank (or single-rank sub-communicator) grid.

Guard the zero-size transfer; a zero-byte copy is a no-op and the
vectors stay empty for the rest of the object's life.

Applied from the Grid source root (containing Grid/): patch -p1.

--- a/Grid/stencil/Stencil.h
+++ b/Grid/stencil/Stencil.h
@@ -884,7 +884,9 @@
 	}
       }
     }
-    acceleratorCopyToDevice(&surface_list_host[0],&surface_list[0],surface_list_size*sizeof(int));
+    if (surface_list_size > 0) {
+      acceleratorCopyToDevice(&surface_list_host[0],&surface_list[0],surface_list_size*sizeof(int));
+    }
     //    std::cout << GridLogMessage<<"BuildSurfaceList size is "<<surface_list_size<<std::endl;
   }
   /// Introduce a block structure and switch off comms on boundaries
